<section class="im-section im-wrap"><div class="im-prose">
<h2>The stack</h2>
<p>A face, one claim, the numbers that back it, a way in — then the story as <code>im-journey</code>: each chapter is a card that <strong>sticks under the bar</strong> as it arrives and stays while the next slides up over it, one step lower, so the years pile up along the top of the window like the tabs of a file. The step is the height of the card's head row, so what peeks out of every card underneath is exactly its year. On a phone the cards simply follow one another.</p>
<p>The rail is pinned beside it: <code>im-journey-index</code> lists the chapters, and the one in view wears the system's "you are here" state — set by a few lines of script that watch the cards and also sweep on scroll, because an observer never fires in a tab that is not being painted. Then Now, Hire me, Elsewhere and the letter, as on every page with a rail.</p>
<div class="im-table-scroll">
<table>
	<thead><tr><th>Class</th><th></th></tr></thead>
	<tbody>
		<tr><td><code>im-journey</code></td><td>The stack. <code>--im-journey-step</code> is the peek (2.75rem); <code>--im-journey-top</code> where the first card sticks.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>im-journey-card</code></td><td>A chapter: <code>im-journey-head</code> (<code>time</code> + a badge), <code>h3</code>, <code>p</code>, an optional <code>img</code> that sits beside the words from 48rem.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>im-journey-index</code></td><td>The years in the rail; <code>data-im-journey</code> names the stack it follows. <code>aria-current="true"</code> is the fill.</td></tr>
	</tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div></section>

{{#contentFor "scripts"}}
<script>
/* The journey index: the chapter in view wears aria-current. An observer
   and a throttled sweep — the sweep is the one that works in an unpainted
   tab, and on a page that opens already scrolled. */
(() => {
	for (const nav of document.querySelectorAll('[data-im-journey]')) {
		const stack = document.querySelector(nav.dataset.imJourney);
		if (!stack) continue;
		const cards = [...stack.querySelectorAll('.im-journey-card')];
		const links = [...nav.querySelectorAll('a[href^="#"]')];
		const mark = () => {
			const line = innerHeight * 0.4;
			let current = cards[0];
			for (const c of cards) if (c.getBoundingClientRect().top <= line) current = c;
			for (const a of links) {
				if (a.getAttribute('href') === `#${current?.id}`) a.setAttribute('aria-current', 'true');
				else a.removeAttribute('aria-current');
			}
		};
		let pending = false;
		const queue = () => pending || ((pending = true), requestAnimationFrame(() => ((pending = false), mark())));
		addEventListener('scroll', queue, { passive: true });
		addEventListener('resize', queue, { passive: true });
		if ('IntersectionObserver' in window) new IntersectionObserver(queue, { threshold: [0, 0.5, 1] }).observe(stack);
		setTimeout(mark, 60);
		mark();
	}
})();
</script>
